  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Use case: dissiminatrions through different xslt's which are all datastreams of one \"xslt object\". Some of the xslt's import and/or include others.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "At present, the only reliable way to do this is e.g. <xsl:import=\"/fedora/get/aux:xslt/XSLT2\"/>.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "A better and more robust solution would be something like <xsl:import=\"$THIS$/XSLT2\"/> or just <xsl:import=\"XSLT2\"/>.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(The first solution is used for the Schema extension of DS-COMPOSITE, the second actually worked in Fedora3.0 but not in 3.4)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "related discussion: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://permalink.gmane.org/gmane.comp.cms.fedora-commons.user/5711"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
