  "description": "<p>Use case: dissiminatrions through different xslt's which are all datastreams of one \"xslt object\". Some of the xslt's import and/or include others.</p>\n\n<p>At present, the only reliable way to do this is e.g. &lt;xsl:import=\"/fedora/get/aux:xslt/XSLT2\"/&gt;.<br/>\nA better and more robust solution would be something like &lt;xsl:import=\"$THIS$/XSLT2\"/&gt; or just &lt;xsl:import=\"XSLT2\"/&gt;.<br/>\n(The first solution is used for the Schema extension of DS-COMPOSITE, the second actually worked in Fedora3.0 but not in 3.4)</p>\n\n<p>related discussion: <a href=\"http://permalink.gmane.org/gmane.comp.cms.fedora-commons.user/5711\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://permalink.gmane.org/gmane.comp.cms.fedora-commons.user/5711</a></p>",
